```
try {
  final response = await request();
  final data = response.data;
  if (data == null) {
    return left(const Failure.malformedResponse(message: 'Empty response body'));
  }
  return right(data);
} on DioException catch (e) {
  return left(_mapDioException(e));
} catch (e) {
  return left(Failure.malformedResponse(message: e.toString()));
}
```
The generic `catch (e)` (not just `on DioException`) guarantees every exception, Dio or otherwise, is mapped to `Left<Failure>`. A doc comment at api_client.dart:21 states this explicitly: "no dio/native exception ever escapes unmapped (RNF09)."

Checked 3 callers — none wrap `_apiClient.get` itself in try/catch; their try/catches are only around local JSON decoding of the already-unwrapped success value:
